    "created_at": "2017-04-23T13:01:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-04-23T13:01:05Z",
    "body": "I think that any event types that are in actively-developed specs should have constructors defined to match other events in the platform.  If that's too much trouble, they can be left in createEvent.  E.g., I don't know if anyone wants to bother getting errata issued for SMIL 3.0 to get a constructor put in the spec there, so if no wants to, I think that should be added to createEvent officially, assuming we consider SMIL 3.0 to be part of the platform.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
